Let f: X ⊆ R² -> R be a scalar-valued function of two variables. 
he level curve at height c of f is the curve in R² defined by he equation f(x, y) = c, where c is a constant. 
In mathematical notation, 

	Level curve at height c = {(x, y) ∈ R² | f(x, y) = c}. 

The contour curve at height c of f is the curve in R³ defined by the two equations z = f(x, y) and x = c. 
Symbolized, 

	Contour curve at height c = {(x, y, z) ∈ R³ | z = f(x, y) = c}
